lause is the carried-approval path: re-presented with approved == true, this rule steps aside.","when":"permission_class == 'NETWORK_WRITE' && !approved"},{"effect":"pre_approved","id":"fixture-fills-standing-approval","note":"Standing approval, bounded by the expression itself: local writes on the fixture host are pre-approved. The same write on any other host falls through.","when":"permission_class == 'WRITE_LOCAL' && payload.host == 'fixture.test'"},{"effect":"pre_approved","id":"docs-writes-pre-approved","note":"Standing approval for documentation writes, bounded by the path prefix in the rule itself.","when":"kind == 'fs.write' && startsWith(payload.path, 'docs/')"},{"effect":"allow","id":"allow-read-only","note":"Reads flow without asking.","when":"permission_class == 'READ'"},{"effect":"allow","id":"allow-carried-approvals","note":"Anything a human has already approved at the gateway level may proceed.","when":"approved"},{"effect":"allow","id":"allow-person-deploys","note":"A person at the keyboard may deploy; a routine may not (routines-ask-on-deploys, the stricter tier, wins for routines).","when":"permission_class == 'DEPLOY' && initiator == 'person'"}]},"version":1}